{
  "0": [
    {
      "text": "Nobody buys silver at spot.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.62
    },
    {
      "text": "Here is what the markup really pays for, and when it is too much.",
      "startSec": 1.4700000000000002,
      "endSec": 5.52
    }
  ],
  "1": [
    {
      "text": "A 1 oz American Silver Eagle typically runs about 20 percent over spot.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 4.117379912663755
    },
    {
      "text": "Spot at 32 dollars means roughly 38 dollars and 40 cents at checkout.",
      "startSec": 3.967379912663755,
      "endSec": 7.9687772925764175
    },
    {
      "text": "That gap is the premium.",
      "startSec": 7.9687772925764175,
      "endSec": 9.360567685589517
    },
    {
      "text": "It covers minting, dealer overhead, insured shipping, and profit.",
      "startSec": 9.360567685589517,
      "endSec": 13.28
    }
  ],
  "2": [
    {
      "text": "The premium does not follow the chart.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.7733333333333334
    },
    {
      "text": "It follows physical demand.",
      "startSec": 1.6233333333333335,
      "endSec": 2.8833333333333337
    },
    {
      "text": "When buyers rush in faster than mints can produce, premiums climb even while spot falls.",
      "startSec": 2.8833333333333337,
      "endSec": 6.99
    },
    {
      "text": "Two purchases at the same spot price can cost very different amounts weeks apart.",
      "startSec": 6.99,
      "endSec": 10.92
    }
  ],
  "3": [
    {
      "text": "Bars are the cheap way to buy ounces.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.9505990783410139
    },
    {
      "text": "A 10 oz bar runs 4 to 6 percent over spot.",
      "startSec": 1.800599078341014,
      "endSec": 4.01479262672811
    },
    {
      "text": "Generic 1 oz rounds run 5 to 8.",
      "startSec": 4.01479262672811,
      "endSec": 5.6490783410138246
    },
    {
      "text": "Government coins like Eagles run about 20.",
      "startSec": 5.6490783410138246,
      "endSec": 7.863271889400921
    },
    {
      "text": "Same silver.",
      "startSec": 7.863271889400921,
      "endSec": 8.49589861751152
    },
    {
      "text": "The difference is minting cost and brand recognition.",
      "startSec": 8.49589861751152,
      "endSec": 11.44
    }
  ],
  "4": [
    {
      "text": "Small coins flip the math completely.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.114285714285714
    },
    {
      "text": "A one tenth ounce coin can run 130 percent over spot.",
      "startSec": 1.964285714285714,
      "endSec": 4.992857142857142
    },
    {
      "text": "The 1 oz version of the same coin runs about 12.",
      "startSec": 4.992857142857142,
      "endSec": 7.735714285714284
    },
    {
      "text": "The smaller the product, the bigger the premium per ounce.",
      "startSec": 7.735714285714284,
      "endSec": 11.2
    }
  ],
  "5": [
    {
      "text": "This is the whole premium picture in one chart.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.3692193308550187
    },
    {
      "text": "Eagles run about 20 percent over spot.",
      "startSec": 2.2192193308550188,
      "endSec": 4.134758364312268
    },
    {
      "text": "Generic rounds about 7.",
      "startSec": 4.134758364312268,
      "endSec": 5.294163568773235
    },
    {
      "text": "Ten ounce bars about 5.",
      "startSec": 5.294163568773235,
      "endSec": 6.453568773234202
    },
    {
      "text": "If your goal is the most ounces for your money, bars win.",
      "startSec": 6.453568773234202,
      "endSec": 9.326877323420074
    },
    {
      "text": "If you want recognizability when you sell, Eagles earn part of that premium back.",
      "startSec": 9.326877323420074,
      "endSec": 13.56
    }
  ],
  "6": [
    {
      "text": "Most dealers list two prices.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.6585123966942148
    },
    {
      "text": "Card and PayPal orders cost about 4 percent more than check, wire, or eCheck.",
      "startSec": 1.5085123966942149,
      "endSec": 5.912148760330578
    },
    {
      "text": "On a 1,000 dollar order that is 40 dollars for the convenience of plastic.",
      "startSec": 5.912148760330578,
      "endSec": 10.144214876033057
    },
    {
      "text": "Shipping works the same way.",
      "startSec": 10.144214876033057,
      "endSec": 11.745537190082644
    },
    {
      "text": "Small orders carry the cost badly.",
      "startSec": 11.745537190082644,
      "endSec": 13.84
    }
  ],
  "7": [
    {
      "text": "Here is the part nobody tells beginners.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.1559322033898307
    },
    {
      "text": "When you sell, dealers pay near spot, sometimes 1 to 3 percent under it.",
      "startSec": 2.005932203389831,
      "endSec": 5.886610169491526
    },
    {
      "text": "You do not get the premium back.",
      "startSec": 5.886610169491526,
      "endSec": 7.611355932203391
    },
    {
      "text": "A 20 percent premium going in means spot has to rise about 20 percent before you break even.",
      "startSec": 7.611355932203391,
      "endSec": 12.72
    }
  ],
  "8": [
    {
      "text": "Run this check on every quote.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.8364372469635626
    },
    {
      "text": "Take the all-in total including shipping.",
      "startSec": 1.6864372469635627,
      "endSec": 4.196234817813766
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide by the troy ounces.",
      "startSec": 4.196234817813766,
      "endSec": 5.787813765182187
    },
    {
      "text": "Subtract spot, then divide by spot.",
      "startSec": 5.787813765182187,
      "endSec": 7.930323886639677
    },
    {
      "text": "A 38 dollar 40 cent coin at 32 dollar spot is 20 percent.",
      "startSec": 7.930323886639677,
      "endSec": 11.419554655870446
    },
    {
      "text": "Ten seconds, and you know exactly what you are paying for.",
      "startSec": 11.419554655870446,
      "endSec": 15.12
    }
  ],
  "9": [
    {
      "text": "Follow for more silver news.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.16
    }
  ]
}